<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/compare" class="link text-sm font-bold">← Comparisons</a>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-6">{a.name} vs {b.name} for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Head-to-head for abandoned cart recovery: timing, channel mix, margin-safe incentives, and Shopify checkout context. Pair test AOVs: $163 and $485.</p>
      <div class="mt-10">
        <TldrBox picks={[{ label: 'Pick A', tool: a.name, reason: a.tagline }, { label: 'Pick B', tool: b.name, reason: b.tagline }, { label: 'Lifecycle layer', tool: 'Sequenzy', reason: 'Strategy and suppression orchestration first.' }]} />
      </div>
      <div class="mt-12 card overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>{a.name}</th><th>{b.name}</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Larger DTC brands with high SMS volume</td><td>Budget-conscious stores needing practical campaigns</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Pricing</td><td>Custom enterprise pricing</td><td>Free tier; paid from ~$25/mo</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Shopify depth</td><td>Deep</td><td>Integration</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Automation</td><td>Advanced</td><td>Solid</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cart channels</td><td>sms, email, marketing, cart recovery</td><td>email, sms, marketing</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Rating</td><td>4.6/5</td><td>4.5/5</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <p>Illustrative proposals throughout the scenarios, notes and deep dives below: timings and caps are test inputs, not observed results or verified capabilities of either supplier. Model contribution as AOV × (margin − discount), with unchanged product cost; discount loss is AOV × discount. These figures exclude additional shipping, payment, messaging and return costs. Before every queued action, check current purchase, refund, stock and suppression state and permission for that channel and marketing purpose. Assign one queue owner, pause overlapping flows, and deduplicate replayed events by cart, customer and action; test those checks before enabling any channel.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Brevo: scenario 1 — international shipping quote sticker shock. At $163 AOV and 38% margin, full-price recovery contributes $61.94 vs $39.12 after a 14% code (Δ $22.82). Ladder touch 1 favors no-discount assist; watch for discount on email one before trust proof. Email 1 ~101m, email 2 ~39h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Brevo: scenario 2 — subscription toggle left on at checkout. At $163 AOV and 38% margin, full-price recovery contributes $61.94 vs $39.12 after a 14% code (Δ $22.82). Ladder touch 2 favors email proof; watch for SMS after 9pm local without quiet hours. Email 1 ~101m, email 2 ~39h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Brevo: scenario 3 — first-time mobile shopper on Instagram traffic. At $163 AOV and 38% margin, full-price recovery contributes $61.94 vs $39.12 after a 14% code (Δ $22.82). Ladder touch 3 favors SMS urgency; watch for no suppression after partial refund. Email 1 ~101m, email 2 ~39h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Brevo: scenario 4 — size matrix with two variants OOS. At $163 AOV and 38% margin, full-price recovery contributes $61.94 vs $39.12 after a 14% code (Δ $22.82). Ladder touch 4 favors push nudge; watch for attribution credit on would-have-returned orders. Email 1 ~101m, email 2 ~39h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Brevo: scenario 5 — gift message field abandoned mid-flow. At $163 AOV and 38% margin, full-price recovery contributes $61.94 vs $39.12 after a 14% code (Δ $22.82). Ladder touch 1 favors no-discount assist; watch for recovery for fully OOS cart. Email 1 ~101m, email 2 ~39h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Brevo: scenario 6 — high-AOV cart with financing widget opened. At $163 AOV and 38% margin, full-price recovery contributes $61.94 vs $39.12 after a 14% code (Δ $22.82). Ladder touch 2 favors email proof; watch for duplicate SMS and email within 20 minutes. Email 1 ~101m, email 2 ~39h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Brevo: scenario 7 — bundle discount not applied in cart. At $163 AOV and 38% margin, full-price recovery contributes $61.94 vs $39.12 after a 14% code (Δ $22.82). Ladder touch 3 favors SMS urgency; watch for welcome discount stacking with cart code. Email 1 ~101m, email 2 ~39h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
